  "review_summary": "Thorough independent external audit of 9702_m22_42 Question 5 covering all 4 leaves: (a) capacitor stored energy calculation E = 1/2 QV = 4.8e-4 J (2 marks, C1 + A1); (b)(i) derivation showing discharge circuit time constant tau = RC = 220e3 * 1.5e-5 = 3.3 s (2 marks, C1 + A1); (b)(ii) multi-step exponential discharge determination linking E proportional to V^2 to find V = V0 / 3 and solving e^(-t/3.3) = 1/3 to yield t = 3.6 s (4 marks, C1 + C1 + C1 + A1); (c) qualitative deduction that adding an identical capacitor in parallel doubles the capacitance and therefore doubles the time constant (2 marks, M1 + A1). All syllabus learning outcomes, skill taxonomy, formula registries, pedagogical hints, walkthroughs, response schemas, and AI rubric criteria strictly comply with CAIE A-Level physics standards.",
